  "reason": "The records collectively provide the main conceptual ingredients. R4 directly demonstrates combined high-pressure/high-temperature treatment as a means of inducing structural transformation in an HEA, while R2 and R11–R15/R19 establish related pressure-assisted thermal processing routes. R6 supplies the closely related lamellar FCC/B2 Al–Co–Cr–Fe–Ni eutectic starting system. R10 shows that coherent nanoscale structures can form in closely related AlxCoCrFeNi alloys, R18 demonstrates hierarchical phase decomposition in a nearby Al–Co–Cr–Fe–Ni composition, and R1 most directly links coherent, multiscale structures to simultaneous strength and ductility. Other records support relevant dislocation, stacking-fault, twinning, precipitation, and interface-controlled mechanisms. An expert could therefore plausibly combine HPHT-induced phase transformation with coherent hierarchical microstructure design in the eutectic alloy, although the exact hexahedron-anvil conditions and detailed FCC-to-B2 dislocation-transfer mechanism are not explicitly disclosed."
